## Claims

### C1 — Diff stays on DE/HARN emit/smoke — PASS
Implementer owned `git diff --stat`: `check_hash.oo`, `cli_emit.oo`, `llvm_emit.oo`, `llvm_emit_binop.oo`, `llvm_emit_call.oo`, `llvm_emit_control.oo`, `llvm_emit_env.oo`, `llvm_emit_expr.oo`, `llvm_emit_fn.oo`, `llvm_emit_let.oo`, `llvm_emit_method.oo`, `llvm_emit_preamble.oo`, `llvm_emit_stmt.oo`, `llvm_emit_ty.oo`. New/expanded: `oodac/llvm_fntab.oo`, `oodac/llvm_link_shim.oo`, `oodac/llvm_emit_mainargs.oo`, `scripts/open68_link_smoke.oo`. Working tree `oodac/main.oo` lines 234–245 dispatch `emit-graph` / `emit-mods` (omitted from that owned stat; still oodac DE). `check_hash.oo` is an 8-line check-path tweak (`byte_at` / `bytes_len` for tab/newline), not org `std/` or `cli/pkg*`. Caps remain: `cli_emit.oo` `&FsCap`/`&SysCap` (line 160); `llvm_emit_fn.oo` still grants `oo_cap_grant_fs` / `oo_cap_grant_sys` (lines 190–195). No dropped `&Cap`.

### C2 — Academy headers and 256-line law — PASS
`llvm_fntab.oo` 193 lines. `llvm_link_shim.oo` 72. `llvm_emit_mainargs.oo` 36. `scripts/open68_link_smoke.oo` 69. Each has Title (`// # …`), Logline, Setup, Beats. Edited emit files stay <= 256: `llvm_emit_fn.oo` 256, `llvm_emit_expr.oo` 256, `llvm_emit_call.oo` 255, `cli_emit.oo` 216, `main.oo` 252.

### C3 — Per-module emit is real — PASS
`open68-mods/list.txt` is 182 graph paths (`oodac/lex_scan.oo` … `oodac/main.oo`). Directory is 183 `*.ll` + `list.txt` (182 modules + `_shim.ll`). Not one concat: `scratch/concat.ll` is `ERR	check	source exceeds 1MiB expanded limit`. Host has no `/usr/bin/llvm-link`. Driver: `cli_emit.oo` `run_emit_llvm_mods` (line 160) writes `list.txt`, `_shim.ll`, and one `.ll` per `load_expand` path. `oodac_main.oo.ll` defines `@main` (line 112) and calls `@parse_cli_argv`; define lives in `oodac_cli_parse.oo.ll` line 92.

### C4 — String names unique — PASS
`llvm_emit.oo` lines 49–51 prefix the pool with `sha256(src)[:12]`. `llvm_emit_env.oo` lines 126–129 emit `@.str.<pfx>.<n>` when set. No unprefixed `@.str.0` in `open68-mods/*.ll`. Sample: `@.str.ff60001b2a34.*` only in `oodac_check_hash.oo.ll`; `@.str.bf6a341ce31a.*` only in `oodac_check_cache.oo.ll`. Hello fixture IR still uses local `@.str.0` (single-file emit; not in the link set).

### C5 — Linked ELF named; ran check fixtures/hello.oo — PASS
Named path: `.ooda-cache/ooda-tmp/oodac_lllink` (`compiler_path.txt`). File is a binary (NUL at ELF pad offset 7). Builder size 2057792 not independently `wc -c` here. `hello_check.log` and `hello_check_2.log` are `OK`. `link_smoke.log` prints `linked check hello OK`, `C emit plus gcc remains product`, `PASSED`. Hostile drop of non-main `oodac_ast_emit_outline.oo.ll` fails ld (`open68_link_drop.err`, `clang_link_hostile.log`: undefined `ast_emit_outline_json` / `ast_emit_outline`). Smoke dest is the side ELF, not `bin/ooda`.

### C6 — No “gcc retired” / “OPEN-68 closed” / gcc-parity — PASS
SHIPPED line 63 still: `Clang link of full oodac via LLVM is residual`. ROADMAP line 142 still: `Clang link of full oodac is next`. Smoke line 67: `C emit plus gcc remains product`. Prior `open68_clangc_smoke.oo` line 72 still: `full oodac clang-link residual`. C emit + gcc path in `cli_emit.oo` `run_emit_c_family` (line 22) is intact. This note does not close OPEN-68.

## Residual (must not be hidden)

  - LLVM emit of `check_listing_fresh` is stubbed to `ret i32 1` (`llvm_link_shim.oo` lines 12–16; call site `llvm_emit_fn.oo` lines 153–160). IR: `oodac_check_hash.oo.ll` lines 235–238. Source `check_hash.oo` lines 43–102 still walks stamps (`byte_at` 10/9). Stub ignores the listing: empty or stale would still be “fresh”.
  - Linked `check fixtures/hello.oo` OK is that short-circuit (`check_mod.oo` lines 61–63). Nonempty `g_` listing exists: `.ooda-cache/check/g_e77568372ba4e38e` is `fixtures/hello.oo	632:1786742258`. Not a stamp-walk. Not a typecheck of hello. Not gcc-parity.
  - Implementer `gdb.err`: `malloc(): unaligned tcache chunk detected` (full stamp-walk intern-abort claim). Not re-run here.
  - `_shim.ll` maps `process_exit` / `path_exists` / `read_file` / `write_file` / `sys_exec` onto `chs_rt` with sret on 24-byte C returns. `sys_exec` calls `oo_cap_grant_sys` and ignores the incoming cap (`_shim.ll` line 38; `llvm_link_shim.oo` line 63).
  - Inter-module `declare TY @name(...)` remains (`llvm_fntab.oo` line 182; e.g. `oodac_check_mod.oo.ll` lines 66–109).
  - Tree `oodac/oodac` / `bin/ooda` were not this slice’s link dest. `oodac check oodac/main.oo` log is `OK` elapsed 5.34s (`check_main.time`). Hello LLVM substance: `hello.ll` `@.str.0` is `Hello, `; `hello_llvm.log` is `Hello, openOODA Developer!`.

## Verdict
PASS on the slice as written. Do not claim a gcc-parity linked oodac. Do not tick OPEN-68 closed.
